  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\nThe failure to expect is **`InvalidCursorError`** from `@ordarium/core` — a dedicated, **fail-closed cursor-rejection error** with:\\n\\n- `name: \\\"InvalidCursorError\\\"`\\n- `code: \\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"`\\n- message: *\\\"The change cursor is not a valid durable position; refusing to guess a resume point\\\"*\\n\\nIt is **not** a generic ledger failure, and **not** `LEDGER_CORRUPT`.\\n\\n## What the cursor is\\n\\nThe \\\"observation cursor\\\" is the opaque durable resume position returned by the state change feed (`StateStore.changes` → `StateChangePage.cursor`), a base64url encoding of `{\\\"c\\\":\\\"<digits>\\\"}` over committed-state-revision commit-observation order (ORD-BOOT-0). The typings call this out explicitly: `StateChangePage` is \\\"One page of committed state revisions in durable ledger commit-observation order\\\". This is the surface exposed to palimpsest through `createStateStore({ runtime })` (`src/effects/runtime.ts:124`, `PalimpsestEffectsRuntime.state`).\\n\\n## Where the rejection is thrown\\n\\nIn the pinned line (`@ordarium/core` / `@ordarium/ledger-sqlite` **1.3.1**; `package.json` + `pnpm-workspace.yaml` overrides, installed version confirmed), `SqliteLedger.changes()` ",
